WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.556
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Friday, October thirtieth.

2
00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:07.475
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.475 --> 00:00:12.101
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:13.682
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.682 --> 00:00:17.289
Two tankers were attacked in the Strait of Hormuz on Thursday.

6
00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:22.329
Dammam flights were disrupted again as the Houthis claim new strikes on Saudi Arabia.

7
00:00:22.329 --> 00:00:24.964
Spain's rail replacement plan has slipped.

8
00:00:24.964 --> 00:00:26.913
And we have a correction on Haiti.

9
00:00:26.913 --> 00:00:29.424
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:29.424 --> 00:00:32.430
Shipping first.

11
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:40.197
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: on Thursday a tanker leaving the Strait of Hormuz was struck by an unknown projectile, with no injuries reported.

12
00:00:40.197 --> 00:00:42.635
Hours later, a second outbound tanker caught fire.

13
00:00:42.635 --> 00:00:47.422
A verified update says a small boat attached two explosive devices to its hull.

14
00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:51.352
The fire is out, the crew is safe, and the ship is under way.

15
00:00:51.352 --> 00:00:54.181
Who carried out the attacks has not been established.

16
00:00:54.181 --> 00:01:03.802
The vessel fire reported in the strait early Thursday local time has since been identified by regional authorities as a dhow involved in a security incident.

17
00:01:03.802 --> 00:01:05.519
It sank, and the crew was evacuated.

18
00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:16.566
The Joint Maritime Information Center's latest weekly assessment, issued before both tanker attacks, rates the threat in the Strait of Hormuz as severe and in the wider Arabian Gulf as substantial.

19
00:01:16.566 --> 00:01:25.011
Tueri suggests that operators with ships in the strait review hull watch and transit timing with their security providers now.

20
00:01:25.011 --> 00:01:26.156
Saudi Arabia.

21
00:01:26.156 --> 00:01:33.612
Claim only: the Houthis say they carried out six attacks on Thursday, including on airports in Riyadh and Dammam and on oil facilities.

22
00:01:33.612 --> 00:01:36.885
Saudi Arabia has not confirmed them.

23
00:01:36.885 --> 00:01:46.154
Reported: the Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted missiles aimed at the east and at Riyadh, and on Friday a drone in the Mecca region, which the Houthis deny launching.

24
00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:51.412
Flightradar twenty-four showed flights holding away from Dammam early Friday local time.

25
00:01:51.412 --> 00:01:53.887
At about five thirty-five a.m.

26
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:57.012
Central, about ten percent of today's Dammam flights were cancelled.

27
00:01:57.012 --> 00:02:07.565
At Riyadh's main airport, about fifteen percent were cancelled, but today's schedule is about a third smaller than yesterday's, so the figures are not comparable.

28
00:02:07.565 --> 00:02:12.486
On Ras Tanura, the Joint Maritime Information Center records a fire at the export terminal on Tuesday.

29
00:02:12.486 --> 00:02:19.489
It says Saudi authorities attributed it to drone debris; the Houthi missile claim remains unconfirmed.

30
00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:20.398
Spain.

31
00:02:20.398 --> 00:02:32.962
Reported, per the state rail operator: its replacement service for the closed Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line will not start before Tuesday, November third, after the train drivers' union required notice for schedule changes.

32
00:02:32.962 --> 00:02:37.362
The line remains closed with no reopening date.

33
00:02:37.362 --> 00:02:38.337
Borders and health.

34
00:02:38.337 --> 00:02:45.684
Confirmed: the amended US Ebola attestation order, covering crew as well as passengers, was published in the Federal Register today.

35
00:02:45.684 --> 00:02:49.335
It applies from eleven fifty-nine p.m.

36
00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.030
Eastern on Tuesday through December eighteenth.

37
00:02:52.030 --> 00:03:04.367
In Nigeria, the disease control center's own protocols, now read directly, say healthy travelers who have been in Congo, Uganda, South Sudan, Burundi or Rwanda are monitored daily for twenty-one days, and anyone with symptoms goes to institutional quarantine.

38
00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.773
These measures are not new.

39
00:03:07.773 --> 00:03:18.712
An undated guideline from the same center describes a twenty-one day self-quarantine for arriving passengers, so whether that covers all arrivals is not clear.

40
00:03:18.712 --> 00:03:20.181
Operations check.

41
00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:21.688
A correction on Haiti.

42
00:03:21.688 --> 00:03:26.545
Yesterday we said the Digicel internet outage was still in place as of early Wednesday.

43
00:03:26.545 --> 00:03:35.012
That was true then, but Georgia Tech's measurements show Digicel's signal returned to pre-outage levels from about nine thirty a.m.

44
00:03:35.012 --> 00:03:37.446
Central on Wednesday, nearly a day before our last episode.

45
00:03:37.446 --> 00:03:38.851
We should have caught that.

46
00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:41.556
We found no Digicel restoration notice.

47
00:03:41.556 --> 00:03:45.152
Moscow's mobile internet limits were scheduled to end Thursday.

48
00:03:45.152 --> 00:03:49.438
We found no extension, though media report some outages continuing.

49
00:03:49.438 --> 00:03:57.379
Power: in Andhra Pradesh, state figures carried by media show about ninety percent of villages hit by Arnab have power back.

50
00:03:57.379 --> 00:04:07.324
Labor: Italian media report the government ordered transport to keep running during today's general strike, so the rail and air walkout warned of yesterday was called off.

51
00:04:07.324 --> 00:04:09.866
British advice still mentions disruption, so check with your operator.

52
00:04:09.866 --> 00:04:15.962
In France, the US government warns of protests today and Saturday.

53
00:04:15.962 --> 00:04:17.422
That's today's brief.

54
00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:20.144
Current as of five forty-five a.m.

55
00:04:20.144 --> 00:04:21.032
Central, Friday.

56
00:04:21.032 --> 00:04:23.497
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

57
00:04:23.497 --> 00:04:28.019
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

58
00:04:28.019 --> 00:04:30.429
Check the original source before you act.

59
00:04:30.429 --> 00:04:39.563
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

60
00:04:39.563 --> 00:04:42.291
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

61
00:04:42.291 --> 00:04:43.640
Thanks for listening.
